; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Palindrome Peeler
; CATEGORY: Recursion
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     recursion, words, palindromes, input, predicates
; SUMMARY:  Checks whether words and whole sentences read the same backwards by peeling matching letters off both ends.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   "racecar" reads the same both ways. To check, compare the first and
;   last letters. If they differ, it is not a palindrome. If they match,
;   peel them both off and check what is left, "aceca", the same way.
;   A word with one letter or none is always a palindrome: that is the
;   stop rule. The program shows the peeling, then lets you type your
;   own words or sentences. Spaces, commas and capitals are ignored, so
;   "Never odd or even" counts.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   1. Press Run. When asked, type a word or sentence in the command box
;      and press Enter. Type quit to finish.
;   2. Put a breakpoint on the line
;        output ispal butfirst butlast :w
;      Run, and watch :w in the Variables panel lose a letter from each
;      end every time you press F5.
;   3. In the Call Stack, the oldest call holds the whole word.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * FIRST, LAST, BUTFIRST and BUTLAST on words
;   * a recursive predicate that outputs true or false
;   * cleaning up input with another small recursive procedure
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Try: step on no pets / a man a plan a canal panama / logo
;   * Make PEEL also print how many letters were compared.
;   * Write a version that checks palindromes of WORDS, so that
;     [fall leaves after leaves fall] counts.
; ============================================================

to ispal :w
  if (count :w) < 2 [output "true]
  if not equalp first :w last :w [output "false]
  output ispal butfirst butlast :w
end

; The same check, printing each layer as it is peeled away.
to peel :w :pad
  if (count :w) < 2 [print (word :pad :w "|  nothing left to compare: yes!|) stop]
  ifelse equalp first :w last :w [
    print (word :pad :w "|  ends match: | first :w)
    peel butfirst butlast :w word :pad "| |
  ] [
    print (word :pad :w "|  | first :w "| is not | last :w "|: no.|)
  ]
end

; Keep only letters and digits, in lowercase. "Never odd, or even!"
; becomes "neveroddoreven".
to tidy :w
  if emptyp :w [output "]
  if memberp lowercase first :w "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789 [
    output word lowercase first :w tidy butfirst :w
  ]
  output tidy butfirst :w
end

to try.phrase
  print []
  print [Type a word or sentence, or quit to stop:]
  localmake "line readlist
  if equalp :line [quit] [print [Goodbye.] stop]
  localmake "w tidy apply "word :line
  ifelse emptyp :w [print [There were no letters in that.]] [
    peel :w "
  ]
  try.phrase
end

peel "racecar "
print []
peel "rotator "
print []
peel "rocket "
print []
print (sentence [Is "Never odd, or even!" a palindrome?] ispal tidy "|Never odd, or even!|)
try.phrase
